Part A — System and workflow design
A.1 Purpose and scope
A.1.1 Purpose
WF-02 lets people reconfirm or question a published accessibility feature at a known AccessMap Location. It tracks independent observations over time, alerts admins to credible changes, and labels information needing recheck. A vote is an observation, not an automatic change to published accessibility truth.
A.1.2 WF-02 at a glance

WF-02 owns both feature-specific CommunityVote and detailed inaccurate-information Report. They are separate records and actions: a Report can describe an incorrect, missing or outdated place/feature fact, while only an eligible CommunityVote participates in vote weighting. A Report never silently becomes a vote; an approved correction to published truth still passes through WF-01 publication.
A.1.3 In scope and out of scope
In scope: authenticated feature-specific CommunityVotes and separately persisted detailed Reports about incorrect, missing or outdated place/feature information; private optional evidence; accuracy-weighted vote assessment; report/dispute moderation; freshness and temporary advisories; authenticated read-only status; audited WF-01 correction handoff and optional reviewed WF-04 events. Reports do not contribute vote weight. Out of scope: creating a Location, directly changing a published LocationFeature from a vote or report, redefining WF-04 tiers, or claiming technical-regulation compliance from an image. A new feature observation or publication correction starts WF-01.
