A.3 Architecture and deployment

This system-wide component view is copied from System Diagrams §3. WF2 uses the API, shared PostgreSQL database, application/domain services and durable Hangfire infrastructure. Text-only vote assessment uses .NET rules without Python; photo/video corrections still enter WF1 verification and Admin publication. A.7/B.3 define the WF2 subset and its cardinalities.
A.4 Preconditions, actions and outcomes
A.4.1 Observation versus publication
A vote can reinforce confidence that a place has not changed, but it does not create a SubmissionClaim: that WF-01 table requires an immutable SubmissionId and belongs to submission evidence. WF-02 persists separate votes. A conflicting photo/video that could change the published value is attached to a new WF-01 Submission using the existing private upload and AI/Hangfire process; the vote and case link to its ID. An admin correction likewise needs an auditable WF-01-supported submission/publication path.
A.4.2 Business rules and validation outcomes
This quick reference summarizes existing WF-02 decisions in A.9–A.17 and B.5–B.16. Detailed eligibility and moderation rules in those sections remain authoritative.

A.5 Product action mapping

Guest and User see public category labels, approximate corroboration age, approved metadata/feature history and Approved CommunityComments. Only User may vote/report/comment or inspect owned private status. Vote comments, voter IDs, individual reputation, device GPS, pending/rejected reports, deliberation and private evidence links remain private.
