A.7 Domain boundaries and source of truth
WF1 FinalConfidence=(1−beta)×AIConfidence+beta×CommunityAgreement, beta=.40×EvidenceStrength; no history means AIOnly, unavailable AI means null/manual review. It uses assessed published claims only. WF2 vote agreement/freshness never rewrites completed WF1 confidence or published facts.
Cross-workflow integration gate: To let vetted WF-02 votes participate in a future WF-01 community-agreement contribution calculation, first version and update WF-01 B.11 to read both published claims and eligible vetted votes via one shared evidence reader. Deduplicate contributors across both sources per (LocationId, ScopeId, FeatureType) and keep source IDs, weighting, eligibility and decision-time snapshots. Until that shared contract is implemented and tested, WF-02 votes influence WF-02 dispute/freshness indicators only. No hidden second formula changes WF-01 evidence scoring or bypasses mandatory Admin approval.
