A.8.3 Relationship and constraint guide
A.9 Community signal and contributor independence
A.9.1 Meaning of a vote
StillAccurate confirms one published feature value/version. Changed states a proposed Available, Limited or NotAvailable value or gives a concrete change description; Unknown is not a positive vote. Each user can have only one currently effective observation for the same feature version; repeat votes supersede for counting and remain as audit. A person cannot corroborate their own source Submission as an independent observer. Other reports from the same person do not become extra independent votes.
A.9.2 Weighting and review safety
Evaluate current scoped feature/version/source claim. Standing<20 or unavailable metrics holds new votes for review; baseline50 passes conduct eligibility. Eligible weights use raw claim accuracy×history support×recency. No-history users can record observations but have zero automatic weight. Admin validation never invents accuracy or restores standing. Safety evidence can trigger manual review even with zero weight. Exclude source author.
Community agreement/conflict inform Admin review, never publish or prove compliance. Crowd auto-resolution is disabled. Retired tier multipliers and three-high-tier/90%-agreement auto-resolution are not implementation alternatives.
A.10 Freshness and temporary access
A.10.1 Separate clocks
LocationFeature.VerifiedAt is WF-01's recorded publication/verification time; WF-02 never rewrites it when a user taps “still accurate”. FeatureCommunityState.LastTrustedReconfirmedAt is the latest eligible independent corroboration. A published feature with no corroboration uses the publication time as its freshness origin and is explicitly labelled Uncorroborated. A vote on an older published version cannot reset the new version's clock.
A.10.2 Age and label
Default RecheckAfterDays=90. At age ≤90, status can remain Fresh; after that, NeedsRecheck unless independent newer evidence has passed validation. A gradual, non-authoritative FreshnessFactor = 2^(-max(0, ageDays-90)/180) can sort recheck priorities. Neither the label nor factor changes the physical accessibility state, historic AI score, points or QCVN compliance assertions. It is not FeatureConfidence and is never fed back into itself. Offer a privacy-safe public timeline of approved Location metadata changes and published scoped feature versions, with effective time and permitted evidence preview; Admin retains private GPS, report and moderation history. Use an immutable Location metadata history plus a paginated public DTO, handling merged Locations. Show newest approved public CommunityComments by default; vote/report notes are not public comments. Public comments default to newest approved first (CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC). Their relevance weight decays by age: CommentRecencyWeight = 2^(-ageDays / CommentHalfLifeDays), where ageDays is measured from server-side CreatedAt in UTC and CommentHalfLifeDays is a configurable, versioned policy (initial value 30 days). In the MVP, the first page of the approved comment list supplies a short recent-context preview: highlight at most the three newest approved comments whose read-time weight is at least 0.25 (within 60 days under the initial 30-day half-life). If none qualify, show no recent-context preview; the full newest-first list remains available. There is no separate relevance sort in the MVP. Older approved comments remain accessible through pagination. Comment decay never changes a verified feature, vote consensus, contributor points or the separate feature freshness score.
A.10.3 Temporary closure
A verified short-lived blockage gets a TemporaryAccessAdvisory scoped to the affected feature and time window (default maximum 60 days). Public UI can show “lối vào tạm thời bị chặn đến [date]” beside the published feature. Votes and reports continue to be accepted and logged; the advisory can suppress duplicate dispute escalation for the same known condition but cannot conceal a new distinct safety concern or automatically mark a building permanently inaccessible. When it expires, Hangfire removes its public active flag and evaluates the underlying feature; contradictory observations remain available for review.
A.11 State machines
A.11.1 Vote

Rejected here is a vote review state, not a WF-01 SubmissionStatus. An honest contradictory view does not qualify as abuse merely because an admin retains the old fact.
A.11.2 Feature dispute

Every transition writes DisputeDecision/audit with reason and actor. Only ResolvedUpdated requires a published WF-01 source and matching Location/FeatureType. A dispute can reopen as a new case after a material new observation or feature version change; closed cases remain immutable.
A.12 Moderation and publication handoff
The admin compares current publication, history, independent votes, age and authorized source evidence. Actions retain baseline, request evidence, link a contributor-owned WF1 correction, or create an evidence-backed time-limited advisory under B.12. StartReview/ResumeReview and held-vote validation follow B.5/B.8. No ordinary Admin mobile contribution or undocumented equivalent-source bypass exists. Changed accessibility truth is published only through WF1 after an uninvolved Admin approves a real Submission; WF2 reconciles the committed outcome and preserves old-version observations.
Use only WF4 v3-metrics-3 reviewed standing sanctions. Retire legacy −100/tier penalties. Ordinary disagreement, honest mistakes, inconclusive evidence and a later physical change do not establish misconduct.
A.13 Cross-workflow behavior
A.13.1 Detailed inaccurate-information reporting
A signed-in User may submit a WF-02 Report when a published place or feature description is wrong, missing or outdated. The report form records a reason and explanation with LocationId, optional FeatureType and observed feature version; it may reference an owned WF-01 evidence Submission. The backend persists Report and status history with an idempotency key. Report is not a CommunityVote and does not count toward weighted agreement, distinct voter thresholds or direct publication. An Admin reviews the report, requests evidence, links an existing feature dispute when appropriate, or rejects it with reason. When a factual correction is needed, create/link a WF-01 Submission or authorized correction; only WF-01 publication updates LocationFeature and its version. WF-02 returns the report status to its owner and exposes moderation actions only to authorized staff. Repeated or abusive reports are rate-limited and reviewed, without automatic reputation penalties. Reports may also identify a wrong address or pin, a scoped feature, an outdated condition or another concrete inaccuracy; they are never limited to image quality. A Location coordinate correction is an Admin-resolved metadata change request with evidence and old/new address/coordinate history, never an automatic majority pin movement. Report creation does not update public truth, and the same author’s separate vote is counted only once as a vote. WrongAddressOrPin reports may include proposed address/coordinate and evidence as untrusted input; only an Admin metadata correction transaction changes Location.Position. Feature reports and votes identify ScopeId where relevant; a scope-specific report does not change another entrance/floor. Resolution also stores verificationOutcome=ConfirmedValid|ConfirmedInvalid|Inconclusive|Duplicate, findingType=IncorrectAtObservation|ChangedSinceObservation|Other, canonical issue and versioned evidence-backed Admin decision in ReportStatusHistory. Emit ReportResolved atomically. WF4 retains one current report outcome per reporter/issue for audit and awards the earliest novel valid factual place/feature report once; revised decisions compensate prior effects. No report outcome changes ContributionAccuracyRate. Comment-target reports are excluded from all report rewards and affect only AccountStanding after an authorized conduct decision. Closing a report alone proves no correctness. Physical changes preserve historically correct claims. Comments/votes are not claim-accuracy samples.
A.13.2 Report lifecycle and product outcomes
Submitted: the authenticated contributor receives a reportId and can view the report privately. UnderReview: an authorized admin has taken responsibility. AwaitingMoreInfo: an admin requests a specific missing detail; the report remains visible to its owner and can return to UnderReview when evidence arrives. LinkedToDispute: the report has been associated with an existing feature dispute; it is still a separate report and adds no vote weight. Resolved: the admin records an outcome with a source pointer, such as a retained published fact, an expiring advisory, or a WF-01 correction that has actually been published. Rejected: the report is invalid, duplicated without new information, or outside WF-02 scope; save a reviewable reason. Resolved and Rejected are terminal report states; a later new observation creates a new report rather than rewriting history.
A.13.3 Reporting boundaries and feedback
A report may target an Active Location even when the named feature is missing, because missing information is itself a reportable issue. A vote requires a published concrete feature and version; a report does not. A report about a route/navigation error is outside this place/feature reporting contract and must be handed to a separate supported route only if one exists. If the reporter supplies a photo/video, WF-01 owns media validation and immutable Submission evidence; WF-02 links that authorized submission instead of accepting arbitrary URLs. The public map can show an approved, scoped review/advisory label where policy allows, but report text and reporter identity are never published as trusted feature data. A admin cannot mark a feature changed merely by closing a report.
A.14 Durable jobs, retry and transaction model
Creating a vote stores the vote, effective-vote supersession, idempotency record and Pending evaluation request in one PostgreSQL transaction; commit first, enqueue Hangfire afterward. A recurring Hangfire reconciler recovers missed enqueue and expired leases. The job processes one (LocationFeatureId, FeatureVersion) with lock/concurrency control, writes an immutable assessment snapshot and updates the current state atomically. Freshness scans eligible current features in bounded batches, recompute derived age at a fixed evaluatedAt, and write only changed states. Independent notification outbox delivery occurs after commit. No media service, WF-04 RPC, FCM or AI HTTP call runs inside a database transaction; take authorized snapshots before the short write transaction.
A.15 Security, privacy and observability
Require authentication and anti-spam limits for votes. Authorize media intent ownership, validate bytes and limits through WF-01's storage adapter, redact faces for public previews where supported, and expose only short-lived admin access to originals. Treat device location, EXIF, account identity, score, media key and free-form accusation as private. Keep administrator decisions, evaluated input snapshot, policy version and scheduler run IDs for audit. Metrics: vote accepts/rejects, below-threshold pending count, independent-voter distribution, conflict-to-review time, aged features, publish-linked resolution, duplicate retries and stale leases.
A.16 Representative acceptance outcomes
A.17 Baseline settings and deferred policies
A.18 Design summary
The architecture carries forward community reconfirmation, reputation-aware aggregation, conflict review, detailed inaccurate-information Reports and age-based recheck through separate durable entities. A brief vote is not a submission claim, a community ratio is not an AI or regulatory compliance score, and neither age nor a crowd alone rewrites a published feature. The exact implementation and test gates follow in Part B.
Part B — Detailed normative specification
B.0 Implementation authority
B.0.1 Mandatory invariants
B.0.2 Source-to-contract interpretation
The provided WF-02 workflow names Verified, Reinforced, Conflict Reported, Community Under Review and Confidence Decay as a claim lifecycle. They are not inserted into WF-01's SubmissionClaim or SubmissionStatus enums. Here Verified means an existing published WF-01 feature; Reinforced, ConflictReported, NeedsRecheck describe FeatureCommunityState; CommunityUnderReview describes an open DisputeCase. This preserves WF-01's immutable evidence, feature-level truth and state machine.
Cross-workflow implementation baseline: create this module within the new .NET8 Code First solution under WF1 B.0.3–B.0.13. Use the shared defined User/auth, DbContext, repository/UoW, storage, jobs and outbox once; there is no old solution or backfill. Apply Worker→Internal Job API, typed DTOs, configuration, DI, generic bases, scoped IUnitOfWork facade and executable acceptance. The owning Part B defines business policies, routes, final schema and retry budgets. Scenario IDs replace diagram-pair numbering. All SQL/EF business access is API-side; scheduler storage is separately credentialed. Include the module in S01–S08 checkpointed generation and the complete test matrix.
B.1 Scope and naming
Routes use UUID v4 database IDs. LOC-SGC-0102 and AMV-2026-08942 remain display-only BusinessCode strings and are never parsed as UUID. Timestamps are UTC timestamptz; confidence/ratios/factors are numeric values [0,1]. UI percentages are derived when rendered. featureType uses WF-01's enum and status uses its existing Available, Limited, NotAvailable, Unknown mapping. No place-wide vote combines ramp, elevator and entrance into one yes/no result.
B.1.1 Preconditions
Location.Status=Active; matching LocationFeature is published and concrete (CurrentStatus != Unknown); version is supplied or resolved consistently from current row. A Provisional/unpublished Location or missing feature routes to WF-01. A merged Location must follow the canonical MergedIntoLocationId resolution rules before voting. Users authenticate; a session alone is not evidence of physical presence. Unknown or expired advisory does not disable votes.
B.2 Canonical enums and state transitions
public enum CommunityVoteType { StillAccurate = 1, Changed = 2 }
public enum CommunityVoteStatus { Recorded = 1, PendingValidation = 2, Eligible = 3, Rejected = 4, Superseded = 5, Archived = 6 }
public enum FeatureCommunityLabel { Uncorroborated = 1, Fresh = 2, Reinforced = 3, NeedsRecheck = 4, ConflictReported = 5, CommunityUnderReview = 6 }
public enum DisputeStatus { Open = 1, UnderReview = 2, AwaitingMoreInfo = 3, CorrectionPending = 4, ResolvedBaseline = 5, ResolvedUpdated = 6 }
public enum InaccurateReportStatus { Submitted = 1, UnderReview = 2, AwaitingMoreInfo = 3, LinkedToDispute = 4, Resolved = 5, Rejected = 6 }
public enum InaccurateReportReason { IncorrectFeature = 1, MissingFeature = 2, OutdatedInformation = 3, Other = 4, WrongAddressOrPin = 5, CommentViolation = 6, MisleadingEvidence = 7, DuplicateLocation = 8 }
public enum DisputeDecisionType { RequestEvidence = 1, RetainBaseline = 2, LinkCorrection = 3, RecordPublication = 4, CreateAdvisory = 5, StartReview = 6, ResumeReview = 7, SeriousEvidenceOverride = 8 }
Preserve existing numeric values. StartReview records Open→UnderReview; ResumeReview records CorrectionPending→UnderReview after failed/superseded correction or renewed review, and AwaitingMoreInfo→UnderReview after evidence receipt. Each has actor, nonblank reason, current version, audit and replay guards. SeriousEvidenceOverride records the Admin opening action; it is not a feature/publication verdict. DisputeCase.OpeningMode is Threshold|AdminOverride; DisputeDecision adds nullable EvidenceSubmissionId FK and EvidenceReportId FK with RESTRICT, required evidence on override. Retain the frozen ratio/headcount/version snapshot in the existing assessment/audit context.
public enum AdvisoryStatus { Scheduled = 1, Active = 2, Expired = 3, Revoked = 4 }
public enum AssessmentJobStatus { Queued = 1, Processing = 2, RetryScheduled = 3, Completed = 4, Failed = 5 }
Stored numeric values are migration-stable. Transitions are only made through the applicable domain service with actor/reason and optimistic concurrency; clients cannot post enums that set review status, eligibility or advisory status. A superseded vote does not alter a closed historic dispute; the current version's assessment is recalculated.
B.3 PostgreSQL schema and relationships
Use the same new PostgreSQL/PostGIS database, EF Core8/Npgsql8 configuration and UnitOfWork as WF1. Application-created primary keys are UUIDv4; User IDs are trusted Supabase subjects. Source/audit FKs use RESTRICT. InitialCreate contains final indexes and scope/history schemas before first write; the optional future WF1/WF2 evidence-reader integration remains disabled.
B.3.1 CommunityVote — append-only observation
Indexes: (LocationFeatureId,ObservedFeatureVersion,CreatedAt DESC), (VoterId,LocationFeatureId,ObservedFeatureVersion,CreatedAt DESC), (EvidenceSubmissionId) filtered non-null. A partial unique index on (VoterId, LocationFeatureId, ObservedFeatureVersion) WHERE Status IN (Recorded, PendingValidation, Eligible) prevents two simultaneous effective candidates. Insert a replacement by superseding the prior active row inside the same transaction before inserting the new row. Use a row lock keyed by user/feature/version or a bounded unique-conflict retry. Never delete the earlier row to resolve uniqueness.
Publication-version identity is (LocationFeatureId, ObservedFeatureVersion); TargetSubmissionClaimId validates that version's source and is not a substitute feature identity. InitialCreate creates this final feature/version-based partial unique index directly on the empty database. Generate no legacy duplicate reconciliation or old-index replacement phase. Runtime replacement/superseding preserves earlier observations and remains atomic under this index. Merge retires/replaces old baselines under WF1 B.7.2 and archives Eligible votes with history; Recorded/PendingValidation observations on retired baselines are historical/non-counting and cannot be validated or retargeted. A fresh vote on the canonical feature uses its current ID/version and is independently eligible; no old confirmation is transferred.
Vote target constraint: TargetSubmissionClaimId equals the source claim of the submitted LocationFeatureId/ObservedFeatureVersion; resolve retained versions through LocationFeatureHistory. Reject a new vote on stale/unpublished targets; archive old-version observations without retargeting. Retain self-observations only as auditable zero-independent-weight records. InitialCreate enforces the final target/version indexes, with no data migration.
B.3.1.1 CommunityVoteStatusHistory — append-only validation audit
Index (CommunityVoteId,CreatedAt). A manual change from pending to eligible must be explainable from this table; the vote row retains only its current status.
B.3.2 FeatureCommunityState — current, public-safe read model
Unique (LocationFeatureId). Index (Label,FreshnessOriginAt) for scans. This table is a projection, not a replacement for LocationFeature.Confidence or the full audit snapshot.
B.3.3 CommunityAssessment — immutable evaluation snapshot
Index (LocationFeatureId,FeatureVersion,AsOfAt DESC); unique (EvaluationRequestId) prevents a retry from inserting the same assessment twice. No PII-bearing snapshot is exposed to map users. InputsJson also records evaluationJobId, capturedRevision and the frozen asOfAt/policy/source snapshot under B.3.6, so retries and successor evaluations remain distinguishable.
B.3.4 DisputeCase, DisputeCaseVote, DisputeDecision
DisputeCase:
Partial unique (LocationFeatureId,FeatureVersion) WHERE status is Open/UnderReview/AwaitingMoreInfo/CorrectionPending. Index (Status,OpenedAt,Id) supports the admin queue.
DisputeCaseVote:
Unique (DisputeCaseId,CommunityVoteId); this association does not change either vote's value or original server receipt time.
DisputeDecision:
Append-only; update decision requires a new row; admin must have WF-02 permission. CreateAdvisory FK can be bound in a second guarded migration step if both tables are created together.
LinkedCorrectionSubmissionId and CorrectionSubmissionId reference WF-01 Submission, not an invented WF-02 copy. ResolvedUpdated requires the linked Submission to be Published, LocationId and FeatureType matching the case, and LocationFeature.SourceSubmissionId (or its published history event) proving the newly published version came from it. A case cannot resolve by comparing only an AI recommendation or a user's text. Version changes from unrelated authorized publications archive or reopen case after evaluation; no blind close.
B.3.5 TemporaryAccessAdvisory
Partial unique (LocationFeatureId) WHERE status Active, or transactionally revoke prior advisory before activation. Index (Status,EndsAt) for expiry. Keep expired notices for audit. Do not write an advisory without admin authorization and a concrete feature.
B.3.6 FeatureAssessmentJob and replay
Unique (LocationFeatureId,FeatureVersion) WHERE Status IN (Queued,Processing,RetryScheduled) permits one active evaluation job. Under the existing feature/version lock, a genuine input change increments the active job's RequestedRevision; when no active job exists, allocate MAX(RequestedRevision)+1 for that feature/version and create a fresh Queued job. New rows initialize InputSnapshotJson={requestedRevisionAtCreation:<revision>,capturedRevision:null,successorJobId:null}; this is one jsonb column on the existing job, not another job/history table. Before evaluation, the current lease holder persists a complete immutable captured snapshot containing capturedRevision, asOfAt, PolicyVersion and the existing authorized input/source/weight provenance. Read the captured revision and its source inputs from the same consistent bounded database snapshot; never label older input rows with a later mutable RequestedRevision. Capture respects the existing authoritative-score adapter boundary; no remote call occurs under database locks, and incomplete/unavailable input is not a fabricated successful capture. The score adapter exposes WF-04 B.1/B.4's processed effective assessment/counter snapshot and version; Pending/Held assessment revisions do not leak a new verdict into old counters. Once captured, retries of this job use the same snapshot/time/policy and do not replace it with newer votes. requestedRevisionAtCreation and captured inputs stay immutable; only RequestedRevision may advance for later inputs. Copy the captured revision/job identity into CommunityAssessment.InputsJson; EvaluationRequestId=job.Id retains one immutable successful assessment per job. On success, persist its assessment and allowed same-feature/version effects under current-state guards, mark this job Completed and clear its lease/retry fields. If RequestedRevision exceeds capturedRevision, atomically create/coalesce one successor with a fresh ID, AttemptCount=0 and the latest requested revision, after terminalizing the old row so the active-job unique index remains valid. If an already-existing successor is coalesced, keep its ID, AttemptCount and any captured snapshot; never reset them. Never overwrite a newer committed assessment/projection with an older captured revision/asOfAt. Store successorJobId once in the old job's existing InputSnapshotJson metadata in that same transaction, whether a successor was created or coalesced; replay follows that identity even after the successor becomes terminal and cannot create another one. This bookkeeping never alters the frozen captured inputs. Dispatch only after commit. Do not return a successfully evaluated job to Queued or reset its AttemptCount. Reuse the shared IdempotencyRecord's existing response fields for exact vote replay; no artificial SubmissionId or extra receipt table is needed.
B.3.7 Migration order and deletion policy
InitialCreate creates the final WF2 vote/history/state/assessment/review/decision/advisory/job/report/evidence/comment schemas once, with FKs to the shared User/Location/Scope/Submission sources and restrictive audit deletion. Use the one NotificationOutbox with real source-event deduplication. ReportEvidence.LinkedSubmissionId references an authorized owned WF1 Submission; no OwnedMediaId compatibility column or direct report-media upload. New comments/reports/jobs start with their declared initial states and complete snapshots; no historical migration, dual-compatible writer or data backfill is implemented. Persist AwaitingMoreInfo directly with the declared enum identities; do not accept an AwaitingEvidence alias. FeatureAssessmentJob includes InputSnapshotJson before its first execution.
Create final indexes/partial unique guards and initialize new feature read models as Uncorroborated using their actual publication time; no vote or trusted confirmation is fabricated.
Implement read/write/evaluation/freshness modules in S03; execute their initial-state and recovery tests before final delivery. There is no old-data rollout/backfill stage.
If a future WF-01 B.11 shared-reader revision is approved, add eligibility/source provenance and versioned migrations separately; do not rewrite older AI verification snapshots.
B.3.8 InaccurateInformationReport and status audit
Report schema and supplements: B.22.1 is the complete field/constraint definition, B.22.2 owns indexes/retention and B.22.3–B.22.7 own requests, validation, replay and transitions. A Report is separate from a vote and contributes no community weight. ReportEvidence links existing reporter-owned WF1 Submissions; direct report media uploads are unsupported. Links to an editable source pin LinkedSubmissionRevision plus immutable claim/media references at creation. ReportEvidence, vote evidence and correction handoffs retain the revision seen by Admin; a later resubmit never retargets them silently. A new reviewed link/reconciliation may choose the newer revision with history. Publication reconciliation requires the actually published revision/claim; old evidence remains auditable.
LocationMetadataHistory is append-only and uses WF-01 B.3's canonical schema: Id, LocationId, optional ScopeId, ActorUserId or ServiceSubject, SourceReportId/SourceSubmissionId, ProposalHistoryId, RecordKind, ChangeType, Decision, Reason, OldValues/NewValues, EvidenceReferences, SourceHash, LocationVersion, optional ScopeVersion, EffectiveAt and CreatedAt. OldValues/NewValues preserve complete before/after fields and their versions; no duplicate PreviousVersion/NewVersion columns are introduced. A public DTO exposes only approved redacted metadata/feature history. CommunityComment is separate from CommunityVote.Comment: Id, LocationId, optional ScopeId, AuthorId, Body, ModerationStatus, CreatedAt, ApprovedAt, Version; only Approved rows are public. For entrance-anchor updates, LocationMetadataHistory.ChangeType=EntranceAnchor and ScopeId is required; old/new position and Scope.PositionVersion are recorded. A canonical Location pin change instead uses ChangeType=LocationMetadata with ScopeId null and Location.MetadataVersion. Public timeline DTOs distinguish these two changes. CommunityCommentModerationHistory is append-only: Id UUID PK, CommentId FK (RESTRICT), FromStatus, ToStatus, AdminId FK, nonempty Reason, OccurredAt UTC and CommentVersion. Unique(CommentId, CommentVersion) prevents a duplicate moderation edge; the Admin transaction checks expectedVersion, updates CommunityComment.Version and appends one history row atomically. Index(CommentId, OccurredAt, Id) supports audit replay. Only the author may create a bounded comment; public GET returns approved/redacted text and safe age, never vote/report notes. Hide does not erase history. Comment relevance decays in MVP using the versioned CommentHalfLifeDays policy defined in A.10.2 (initial value 30 days), calculated at read time from server-side CreatedAt in UTC. Default public ordering stays newest approved first (CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC); read-time weight qualifies up to three newest approved first-page comments for recent-context emphasis when weight is at least 0.25. No relevance-sort branch exists in the MVP. No batch mutation is needed, older approved comments remain paginated and visible, and comment decay never modifies LocationFeature confidence, votes, contributor points or feature freshness. Add optional server-controlled ConfirmedViolationCategory, ViolationKey, EvidenceReferences and PolicyVersion to CommunityCommentModerationHistory; ordinary approval/hide does not imply sanction. A reviewed sanction requires evidence and an uninvolved Admin. ReportStatusHistory likewise retains verified outcome, canonical issue/violation key, confirmed category and versioned decision. Source/evidence links use RESTRICT; effects reference the actual committed typed decision. Apply WF1's reviewed closure/renovation/replacement rules. Report may signal a change or evidence of closure; closing a report alone never changes Location identity/status. Old comments remain on their original place with history/context; old feature votes/reports retain old version references and cannot establish the replacement business's accessibility. Lifecycle withdrawal may retire obsolete projections through the authorized WF1 Location action, while corrections to published values still require new WF1 approval.

