B.5 User and admin HTTP API
All body field names below use JSON camelCase; status names use consistent PascalCase enum serialization or documented snake-case wire mapping in the existing API. Standard error envelope includes code, message, correlationId and validation details, without private metadata. Authorize all writes server-side. Exact backend route prefix can be adjusted to the existing API versioning convention, but document clients must use one canonical contract.
B.5.1 GET /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/features/{featureType}/community
Guest/User public read uses WF-01 visibility rules and returns published public-safe community state only. Require scopeId and resolve (locationId,scopeId,featureType); return 422 invalid scope and 404 unpublished scoped feature. Return feature/source IDs and published version with separate community status. Never infer another floor/entrance. No token is required for this public projection; mutations and private status remain authenticated.
{
"locationId": "c29efc42-05b9-43d5-bc74-17d616f7eab2",
"scopeId": "<scope-uuid>",
  "locationFeatureId": "<published-feature-uuid>",
  "sourceClaimId": "<published-source-claim-uuid>",
  "featureType": "Ramp",
"publishedStatus": "Available",
"publishedVersion": 2,
"verifiedAt": "2026-06-01T08:00:00Z",
