}
Require scopeId in the body. Resolve LocationFeatureId and current SourceClaimId server-side from (locationId, scopeId, featureType), and reject a stale observedFeatureVersion with 409 rather than retargeting the vote. StillAccurate requires no alternative status; Changed requires a different concrete status or a description of an observed temporary change. A later WF-01 evidence Submission must match location, scope and feature and pass ownership checks. Vote targets the resolved SubmissionClaim; the feature/version records its publication context. Do not accept client weights, tier, timestamps, vote status, storage URLs or mediaIds.
Success 201 Created when saved, regardless of asynchronous aggregation:
{
"voteId": "606427ed-71a6-4ce7-a559-61386388cb44",
"voteStatus": "Recorded",
"evaluationStatus": "Queued",
"featureVersion": 2,
"publishedFeatureChanged": false,
"message": "Đã ghi nhận quan sát. Trạng thái cộng đồng sẽ được cập nhật sau khi đối chiếu."
}
Standing<20 gives PendingValidation; unavailable metrics has a distinct retryable reason. Baseline50 passes conduct gate; zero history gives zero numerical weight without blocking recording. Admin validation changes vote eligibility only, never accuracy/standing. Exact authorized replay precedes mutable-state checks; changed payload→409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED.
B.5.3 POST /api/v1/community-votes/{voteId}/link-submission
Authenticated voter only; header Idempotency-Key. Body {"submissionId":"UUID"}. Validate same contributor, canonical Location, FeatureType, intended claim and non-terminal evidence availability. If a vote already links the same Submission, return previous result; different Submission while an active link exists requires explicit correction policy and cannot silently replace audit. Return 200 with evidenceSubmissionId, link timestamp and evaluationStatus=Queued. This endpoint links, not creates, a WF-01 Submission; the contributor must choose and submit the actual photo/video through WF-01's signed upload and verification pipeline. An unreviewed linked Submission does not make the vote automatically Eligible. Validate ScopeId matches the vote's resolved feature and the linked claim; a different floor/entrance is rejected, even at the same Location.
B.5.4 GET /api/v1/admin/community-disputes
Requires Wf02.Moderate, isAdmin=true and validated Admin Portal session/scope. Query status=open|under_review|awaiting_more_info|correction_pending, page, pageSize, optional Location/Feature filter. Paginated response includes ID, Location public name, FeatureType, published version/value, age, eligible independent voter counts, reason code and openedAt; private observations/media require a separate authorized detail read. GET /api/v1/admin/community-disputes/{caseId} returns case chronology, policy/versioned weight snapshot and authorized evidence references (not public raw URLs). Pagination has deterministic (OpenedAt,Id) order. Manual override creation: POST /api/v1/admin/community-disputes requires current portal Wf02.Moderate permission, Idempotency-Key and {locationFeatureId,observedFeatureVersion,evidenceSubmissionId?,reportId?,reason}. Require at least one real typed evidence source, matching canonical Location/scope/feature and accessible to the uninvolved Admin. A reviewed source may be unpublished evidence; it cannot itself publish a correction. Validate/recheck current feature version and conflicts in the transaction. Create/reuse the active case with OpeningMode=AdminOverride and append SeriousEvidenceOverride decision, evidence FKs and actor/reason/policy/input snapshot atomically. Normal automatic opening uses OpeningMode=Threshold and the .40/two-Changed-voter predicate. Exact replay returns the original case; stale version409, missing/foreign/unsupported evidence422/403 per disclosure policy. An ordinary mobile User cannot use this route.
B.5.5 PATCH /api/v1/admin/community-disputes/{caseId}
Headers: Authorization: Bearer <Admin Portal JWT access token> under WF-01 B.0.13; Idempotency-Key and If-Match version/ETag. Examples:
{
"decision": "LinkCorrection",
"reason": "Ảnh hiện trường cho thấy trạng thái ram dốc cần xác minh lại.",
"correctionSubmissionId": "834e25e1-f07c-4070-9135-6e5fdac07ee6"
}
LinkCorrection changes case to CorrectionPending, not public truth. RecordPublication resolves updated only when that submission was published for the same feature. RetainBaseline resolves baseline with reason; RequestEvidence leaves case AwaitingMoreInfo; CreateAdvisory requires startsAt, endsAt and scoped reason within max duration. Return case ID, status, moderatedBy, decidedAt, publishedFeatureChanged, and optional advisory. A stale If-Match or illegal transition returns 409; no silent last-writer-wins decision.
Additional decisions: StartReview accepts Open; ResumeReview accepts CorrectionPending with a failed/superseded correction or documented need to reconsider, and AwaitingMoreInfo after evidence receipt. Both result in UnderReview and append DisputeDecision without erasing prior links. Preserve correction IDs and previous decisions in audit; replacement of the active correction requires an explicit reviewed LinkCorrection after return to UnderReview. Every PATCH uses current case ETag/If-Match, Idempotency-Key, authorization/conflict-of-interest checks and a nonblank reason. Authorized identical replay precedes state/version checks. Concurrent or unsupported transitions return 409 with no writes.
B.5.6 WF-02 detailed report API
Detailed reports use POST /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/reports with authenticated ownership and Idempotency-Key. They record an issue for review without changing votes or published feature truth. B.22.3 defines the exact create payload/response; B.22.4 defines owner/Admin reads, supplements, metadata and comment routes; B.22.5–B.22.7 define validation, atomic writes and decisions. Use those contracts directly rather than a separate report DTO or state machine.
B.6 Ordered vote processing
Authenticate and authorize; rate-limit repeated votes and reject malformed location/feature UUIDs. Validate the stable request shape, then look up (UserId, endpoint, Idempotency-Key) using the canonical submitted business payload before current feature/version or mutable linked-evidence checks. An authorized matching replay returns stored status/body; changed payload returns 409.
Canonicalize merged Location and load its current published LocationFeature, version and status; enforce the client-observed version with 409 FEATURE_VERSION_CHANGED and return current safe feature summary.
Validate VoteType, proposed state, text length/content, and optional linked Submission subject and ownership. Never trust client reputation or timestamps.
For a new request only, continue after the replay lookup above; preserve the original submitted selector/version in the request hash. Canonicalize current identity for processing, not by changing the identity of a stored replay. Recheck idempotency again under the write transaction and resolve a concurrent unique-key winner by replay/hash comparison.
Resolve WF4 standing and verified-claim counter snapshot outside the write transaction (or use an already consistent local authoritative projection). If unavailable, set PendingValidation and enqueue reevaluation.
Begin short DB transaction; recheck feature version and lock per voter/feature/version; supersede previous active effective vote; append new vote and status audit; create or coalesce FeatureAssessmentJob; store idempotent response; commit.
Best-effort enqueue Hangfire by domain job ID, return 201. Hangfire reconciler recovers a committed job if enqueue fails. Never wait for Python AI or community recomputation in the mobile POST.
B.7 Evidence and media route
A quick vote is intentionally lightweight and has no raw upload fields. A detailed Report is a separate WF-02 record and never becomes a counted vote. The original source's optional evidence_media means open WF-01 contribution with evidence, using POST /api/v1/media/upload-intents, direct private signed PUT and POST /api/v1/submissions, then link the resulting UUID to the vote/case. WF-01 revalidates actual JPEG/PNG/video bytes, GPS/EXIF, ownership, quality and privacy, and Hangfire calls the Python service. WF-02 moderation can view the linked Submission's original evidence only under authorization. Link creation does not copy media to a public bucket, bypass AI or presume its final outcome. If product later requires an upload inside the quick vote form, that is an explicit new upload-intent ownership contract plus migrations, not mediaUrls guessed by the frontend.
B.8 Vote eligibility and independence
B.8.1 Effective observation set
For current feature version v, take the latest non-superseded, non-rejected vote per VoterId targeting its published SourceClaimId, where ObservedFeatureVersion=v. Archived votes never count for v+1. PendingValidation has applied weight zero; Recorded awaits eligibility processing and does not increase public confirmation until validated. Eligible needs successful identity, subject, current-version and policy checks. The baseline source contributor's own quick vote is not an independent confirmation. If a voter also owns a WF-01 published claim for this feature, the later shared-reader extension deduplicates across both sources; no double vote. All lookups and deduplication remain within (LocationId, ScopeId, FeatureType); never pool observations across floors/entrances.
B.8.2 Detecting conflict
Ordinary opening requires weightedTotal>0, weightedConflict>=.40 and at least two distinct independent eligible Changed voters with positive effective weight for the current feature/version; count each once and exclude the source contributor. Pending, superseded, rejected, old-version and zero-weight observations do not satisfy the count. Changed must specify a concrete alternative or observed temporary condition; StillAccurate is agreement, Unknown is not. Insufficient ratio/headcount keeps observations recorded. An uninvolved Admin may explicitly override with serious validated evidence, reason and audit; a user flag or alarming words is insufficient. Reuse an active compatible case/advisory. No automatic truth change or penalty.
B.8.3 Standing and accuracy snapshot
Read standing and verified claim counters with policy. Standing<20 or missing stats holds new votes; Eligible weight=T×min(assessedCount/10,1)×recency, zero history→0. Snapshot all inputs. Keep GET held-vote list/details and POST /admin/community-votes/{voteId}/validation with Idempotency-Key, If-Match, Accept|Reject and reason. Forbid self/involved review; recheck current target, version, independence and evidence under locks. Accept changes eligibility only, appends history and coalesces evaluation; reject becomes Rejected. Replay precedes state checks; stale/superseded votes→409. Safety evidence may open review despite zero numerical weight.
B.9 Recency and weighting
At frozen asOfAt, for each eligible effective independent voter i:
ageDays_i = max(0, (asOfAt - CommunityVote.CreatedAt_i).TotalDays)
recencyWeight_i = 2 ^ (-ageDays_i / HalfLifeDays)
effectiveWeight_i = ContributionAccuracyRate_i × min(AssessedClaimCount_i / AccuracyHistoryTarget, 1)
× recencyWeight_i // no history:0; no standing/reputation multiplier
weightedAgree = sum(effectiveWeight_i where vote_i agrees with published status)
weightedTotal = sum(effectiveWeight_i for all eligible concrete observations)
weightedAgreement = weightedAgree / weightedTotal, if weightedTotal > 0
weightedChanged = sum(effectiveWeight_i for eligible Changed observations)
weightedConflict = weightedChanged / weightedTotal when total>0; otherwise null
If total is zero, weightedAgreement=null, hasIndependentCommunityEvidence=false; never display 100% agreement from zero votes. Count each user once and record distinct positive-weight voters and Changed voters; legacy DistinctHighTierVoters is not a score/threshold authority. Round displayed percentages to one decimal; persist exact numeric snapshots with a deterministic evaluation timestamp. RecentWindowDays=30 is a label/priority window for the newest cohort, not an extra multiplier silently applied on top of the half-life. Historical WF-01 published claims use their own frozen 180-day consensus logic; WF-02's weightedAgreement is a separate value until the B.11 integration gate is accepted.
B.9.1 Example
Example: independent effective weights .8, .2, .5; first agrees and the last two vote Changed. Agreement=.8/1.5=.5333 and conflict=.7/1.5=.4667 with two positive-weight Changed voters: ordinary threshold met. Multiple observations by one person count once. If one Changed voter has zero weight, only one qualifies and the ordinary branch cannot open, even with ratio>=.40; a separately audited Admin serious-evidence override remains possible.
B.10 Freshness algorithm and presentation
freshnessOriginAt = LastTrustedReconfirmedAt ?? CurrentPublishedFeature.VerifiedAt
ageDays = max(0, (asOfAt - freshnessOriginAt).TotalDays)
isStale = ageDays > RecheckAfterDays
FreshnessFactor = 2 ^ (-max(0, ageDays - RecheckAfterDays)
/ FactorHalfLifeAfterRecheckDays)
LastTrustedReconfirmedAt advances only for an independent, eligible, positive-weight, same-version StillAccurate corroboration without active contradictory evidence; a self-confirmation, zero-weight observation or PendingValidation vote never resets it. A linked WF-01 re-publication starts a new version with new VerifiedAt; previous reconfirmations cannot be copied to it. The factor remains 1 until the 90-day recheck date, then decreases gradually, clamped to [0,1]. Set NeedsRecheck when stale and no higher-priority active dispute/advisory; materialized label precedence: CommunityUnderReview > ConflictReported > NeedsRecheck > Reinforced > Fresh > Uncorroborated. An active advisory is a separate overlay and can coexist with a case label; it never converts a published Available feature into NotAvailable.
The UI should say “thông tin cần xác nhận lại” rather than “địa điểm không còn tiếp cận được”. Do not store FreshnessFactor in WF-01 LocationFeature.Confidence, or turn a time-based warning into a claim that an item fails Vietnamese technical regulation QCVN 10:2024/BXD.
B.11 WF-01 shared community-evidence integration gate
Deferred WF1/WF2 cross-source evidence integration is specified in Optional. Current WF1 uses eligible assessed published claims only; WF2 votes retain their own frozen aggregation and never directly enter WF1 confidence.
B.12 Dispute policy and review
B.12.1 Opening and coalescing
Open/reuse one DisputeCase per (LocationFeatureId,FeatureVersion) when weightedConflict>=ConflictRatioThreshold=.40 and MinIndependentVotersForReview=2 distinct eligible positive-weight Changed voters meet independence rules. weightedConflict=weightedChanged/weightedTotal, null for zero total. Alternatively an uninvolved authorized Admin records SeriousEvidenceOverride with nonblank reason, actual evidence reference, actor/time, feature version and frozen weights/denominator/headcount/policy. This override can use a credible report/evidence item even with zero automated weight; user text alone cannot activate it. Link votes and append the opening decision atomically under the one-active-case unique index. Opening never changes a published value or score.
B.12.2 Decisions
RetainBaseline is a finding that the evidence does not support changing current publication; it is not a finding of intentional lying. Do not emit a negative WF-04 event without its independent reviewed misconduct procedure. Admin concurrent decisions compare xmin/ETag and return 409 when stale.
StartReview: Open→UnderReview. ResumeReview: CorrectionPending→UnderReview for an invalid/failed/superseded correction or reasoned renewed review; AwaitingMoreInfo→UnderReview when evidence arrives. Both append the corresponding decision and preserve prior evidence/history. These rows complete the decision table and match System Diagrams 4.4; no unrecorded status assignment is permitted.
B.12.3 Crowd auto-resolution is gated
CrowdAutoResolveEnabled=false is mandatory in v3-metrics-3. Do not persist or compute retired high-tier/90%-agreement auto-resolution candidates. WF2 computes accuracy-weighted agreement/conflict and freshness for review only; an uninvolved authorized Admin resolves a case under evidence, version and audit guards. Changed published feature values require WF1 publication. Any future crowd-resolution proposal belongs to Optional and requires a separate approved contract; deployment configuration alone cannot enable it.
B.13 Temporary advisory lifecycle
The admin checks evidence and sets StartsAt<EndsAt≤StartsAt+MaxDurationDays. Scheduled notice activates by Hangfire at StartsAt; active notice expires by Hangfire at EndsAt, using idempotent UTC comparisons. Optional deliberate Revoked requires a reason and admin identity. Read path also checks StartsAt<=now<EndsAt so a delayed job cannot show an expired notice. An advisory only communicates a time-limited observed obstruction; it does not suspend receiving new community observations, hide the permanent feature version or automatically discard an open case. At expiry, enqueue assessment and put unresolved meaningful conflicts back into the review queue.
B.14 Background jobs and reliability
B.14.1 Vote evaluation job
The vote transaction creates/coalesces the existing FeatureAssessmentJob under B.3.6. After commit schedule Wf02Evaluate(jobId); the Hangfire handler calls POST /api/internal/v1/community-jobs/{jobId}/evaluate through InternalJobApiClient and never accesses business repositories. API-side claim increments this job's AttemptCount and establishes its owner/lease. Persist/reuse InputSnapshotJson before computing at the captured asOfAt and policy; score/provider acquisition remains outside database transactions. Recheck owner, attempt, live database-time lease, feature/version and current assessment guards before committing CommunityAssessment, allowed FeatureCommunityState/case effects and completion. If newer inputs arrived, complete the evaluated job and atomically create/coalesce its successor as B.3.6 specifies, then dispatch after commit; an enqueue failure is reconciled. A changed published feature version keeps old assessments historical and schedules the current version, never retargets an old job's snapshot. Shared service authentication, receipts and deadlines remain WF-01 B.0.4.
B.14.2 Recurring scans and missed enqueue
Register Hangfire recurring Wf02FreshnessScan on a configured daily schedule and Wf02ReconcileJobs initially once per minute. Scan current published features by indexed pagination with a stable cutoff, at most BatchSize rows per transaction. Candidate selection includes approaching/past recheck age, active advisory start/expiry, changed feature version and stale evaluation job leases. Reconciliation re-enqueues Queued, due RetryScheduled and expired Processing jobs; it does not create duplicates through partial unique constraints. Multiple servers must coordinate by DB locking and a cluster-wide Python/CPU budget when a linked WF-01 submission needs inference; the WF-02 evaluator itself never calls Python. Reconciliation also dispatches committed successor jobs. It must not increment RequestedRevision or create a successor merely because a scan/HTTP delivery repeated. A genuinely new vote, eligibility/source/policy-version change or newly due versioned freshness/advisory cutoff is new input; deduplicate the same change/cutoff under the existing feature/version lock.
B.14.3 Retry, failure and observability
Retry budget is per FeatureAssessmentJob.Id: MaxAttempts=3 total started executions, including crash recovery. Claim/reclaim only when AttemptCount<MaxAttempts; increment on each started execution and never reset the counter. Retain the captured InputSnapshotJson across retries. Retryable failure at attempt n<MaxAttempts sets RetryScheduled with NextRetryAt=databaseNow+RetryBackoffSeconds[n-1], clears owner/lease and is scheduled after commit. Disable Hangfire AutomaticRetry so transport/scheduler redelivery cannot multiply this budget. Nonretryable failure or exhausted/expired attempt 3 settles the old job Failed under its current recovery guards, with no fourth execution. If RequestedRevision exceeds the frozen capturedRevision (or requestedRevisionAtCreation when no complete capture exists), terminalize the failed job and create/coalesce one fresh successor for those genuinely newer inputs in the same transaction. If no newer revision exists, remain Failed for authorized recovery; do not clone the same failed inputs into an endless series of fresh jobs. A terminal recovery replay cannot create a second successor. Preserve last safe public truth and expose the failure operationally, never invent Reinforced. Log job/revision/attempt/policy and safe reason codes; redact private comments/raw scores.
B.15 Transaction and concurrency matrix
xmin protects materialized state and dispute cases. Job completion checks feature version and latest queued revision under the same transaction. Stale workers must not close a newer case. Serializable transaction is not globally required if row locks, unique constraints and bounded retries enforce these invariants. PostgreSQL and Hangfire persistence are separate commits even if they share the server; the domain job plus reconciler bridges the gap.
B.16 Error, exception and user response matrix
The original source's below-default reputation EX-01, no-claim EX-02, insufficient-evidence EX-03, false-report EX-04, no-decay EX-05, crowd EX-06 and temporary-closure EX-07 correspond to the specific rows/policies above. EX-04 never deducts points simply because a claim is not confirmed; WF-04 adjudication is separate.
B.17 Security and privacy
Guest and User may read published public-safe projections. Vote/report/comment writes and private status require an active authenticated User with isAdmin=false. Management requires current isAdmin=true, validated Admin Portal session and endpoint action policy. Admin cannot sign in to mobile or use ordinary User write routes. An Admin cannot decide a report or dispute involving their own data: compare the portal-authenticated Admin ID with Report.ReporterId; the ContributorId of the challenged published TargetSubmission or current baseline source Submission; the ContributorId of any linked correction Submission; and the CommunityVote.VoterId of every vote linked through DisputeCaseVote.CommunityVoteId, including OpenedByVoteId. For a report linked to a dispute, apply the same case check. Another uninvolved Admin must review it. Resolve canonical source ownership and make this guard part of the decision transaction so a concurrent link or source-version change cannot bypass it. A one-Admin self-originated case remains in the applicable review state until a different Admin can decide; WF-01 corrections also require an uninvolved authorized Admin's approval in PendingModeration; no automatic publication exception exists. Reuse WF-01 A.2.3 User.isAdmin and session authorization; no Role/UserRole mapping is added. Hide private comments, voter IDs, tier, score, device position, evidence keys and any closed moderation accusations from public APIs. Use WF-01 owned signed uploads only for linked Submission evidence, size/type/byte validation and short-lived admin read capabilities. Record reason and actor for manual eligibility and advisory changes. Rate-limit per user/location/feature with configuration to reduce spam; user identity and stable feature/version dedupe prevent simple repeat voting. A third-party OpenStreetMap/Overpass listing is not a verified accessibility source. Public labels are descriptive and do not claim a feature is compliant with the Vietnamese technical regulation from an image or from crowd counts. Apply WF-01 B.0.13 human JWT, current-session and UserMobile/AdminPortal authorization contracts.
B.18 Notifications and UX text
Reuse WF-01 B.3.17 NotificationOutbox and FCM delivery. Existing dispute/advisory event types are DisputeOpened, EvidenceRequested, DisputeResolvedBaseline, DisputeResolvedUpdated, AdvisoryStarted and AdvisoryExpired. RelatedCaseId is the nullable DisputeCase FK; SubmissionId is required only when the event has a submission source. A report-only evidence request/final decision carries its real reportId in PayloadJson without inventing a case or submission. Supply and validate sourceType/sourceId/sourceEventId under the shared WF-01 B.3.17 allowlist; reportId refers to the Report, while sourceEventId refers to its committed history. Do not impose a submission/case requirement on other supported workflow events. Every event carries the immutable sourceEventId; uniqueness by recipient/type/sourceEventId prevents retry duplicates while allowing later legitimate decisions. Commit outbox work with its source history/outcome, dispatch after commit, and send private outcomes only to involved users. Suggested messages:
Avoid promising reputation credit on an unreviewed quick vote and avoid “địa điểm đạt Vietnamese Technical Regulation” claims. Notification failure cannot roll back a confirmed case transition or WF-01 publication.
B.19 Representative integration test scenarios
Run PostgreSQL integration tests for partial indexes, FK restrictions, xmin and worker leases. Unit-test deterministic weighting at fixed asOfAt; API tests cover auth and no private-field leakage. Test a freshly published WF1 feature without WF2 votes initializes Uncorroborated, with no fabricated consensus.
Add StartReview/ResumeReview and held-vote Accept/Reject tests: every allowed/forbidden source state, stale ETag, concurrent decisions, authorized replay after status change, self-review rejection, preservation of linked evidence/history, no account-score mutation, no resurrection of superseded/old-version votes and one coalesced evaluation job. Every diagram edge maps to a typed action/audit. Canonical merge fixtures preserve source vote/version and never transfer corroboration to a replacement feature automatically.
Merge/version regression: one user may have historical and fresh votes with the same source claim and equal numeric versions on different feature IDs. The feature-based partial unique index permits the fresh vote, while same-feature/version replacement still supersedes exactly one effective candidate. Retired-baseline observations never contribute or regain eligibility; preserve target IDs, history and authorized replay.
Revision/budget tests: hold an evaluation at its third started attempt and commit a new vote; success completes the old job and creates exactly one fresh successor with AttemptCount=0 rather than leaving an unclaimable old Queued row. Verify its captured inputs/time remain unchanged on failure retry; only a genuinely advanced revision/cutoff permits successor creation after exhaustion. Crash before/after snapshot capture and before/after completion commit, vote-versus-completion races, repeated completion/reconciliation and two concurrent voters must preserve one active job, every committed input change and one assessment per job. No new revision means no fourth attempt or unbounded fresh-job loop; stale owners cannot create successors or overwrite newer projections. Verify jobs with missing required snapshot metadata are rejected/reconciled rather than authorized.
B.20 API ownership and acceptance traceability
B.21 Deployment and rollout checklist
InitialCreate includes the full Report/ReportStatusHistory schema and every FK/index/check before any app route runs. A new published feature starts Uncorroborated with its actual version/time; do not seed fictitious independent votes.
Wire the shared LocationFeature read service, existing identity/auth, WF-01 submission/link and WF-04 reputation adapters; verify private media access with the existing storage adapter.
Deploy API read routes; then vote and Report write routes with moderation authorization and shared idempotency; enable the durable vote evaluation job and Hangfire recurring freshness/reconciliation, metrics and operator replay. Run Report transition/replay tests before exposing the Report action in WF-03.
Crowd auto-resolution and WF1 vote integration remain disabled. Reviewed conduct/report events use WF4 v3-metrics-3; no automatic misconduct inference.
Validate backups/migrations, concurrency, unauthorized access, partial unique constraints and outbox delivery; audit that no vote updates WF-01 LocationFeature directly.
B.22 Detailed WF-02 Report implementation contract
This section expands B.3.8 and B.5.6. The existing CommunityVote, DisputeCase, LocationFeature and WF-01 publication contracts remain authoritative. A Report is a separately auditable complaint; no Report status, count or attachment is a consensus vote.
B.22.1 Entities, keys and relational constraints
InaccurateInformationReport columns: Id UUID v4 PK; LocationId UUID FK to the canonical existing Location; TargetType enum Location|Feature|Submission|Comment; CommentId nullable FK to CommunityComment (RESTRICT), required only for TargetType=Comment; ReportedCommentVersion nullable integer required for Comment; ReportedCommentSnapshot jsonb nullable, required only for Comment and server-populated with the reported body, version, author and capture time. Retain this immutable snapshot privately for review. Derive TargetType for compatible existing factual-report requests; Comment requests explicitly identify CommentId. Comment must belong to the same canonical Location. Comment targets require Reason=CommentViolation and null feature/submission/dispute/correction/proposed-address fields; LocationFeatureId nullable FK and ObservedFeatureVersion identify the feature version being reported; TargetSubmissionId and TargetSubmissionClaimId nullable FKs identify the challenged published source; ReporterId UUID FK to existing User; ScopeId nullable FK to AccessScope of the same Location; ProposedAddress and ProposedPosition nullable only for WrongAddressOrPin; FeatureType nullable using WF-01's canonical feature enum; ObservedFeatureVersion nullable integer; Reason required enum IncorrectFeature, MissingFeature, OutdatedInformation, WrongAddressOrPin, Other, CommentViolation, MisleadingEvidence or DuplicateLocation; Description required bounded text; Status required enum Submitted, UnderReview, AwaitingMoreInfo, LinkedToDispute, Resolved or Rejected; LinkedDisputeCaseId nullable FK; LinkedSubmissionId nullable FK; Version integer concurrency token initialized to 1; CreatedAt and UpdatedAt UTC. Typed target constraints: Submission requires TargetSubmissionId to an actually Published same-Location submission and publicly visible approved source evidence; optional TargetSubmissionClaimId narrows it to an approved claim, with matching ScopeId. Do not expose private pending/rejected submissions. Fixed reasons: Feature=IncorrectFeature|MissingFeature|OutdatedInformation|Other; Submission=IncorrectFeature|OutdatedInformation|MisleadingEvidence|Other; Location=WrongAddressOrPin|DuplicateLocation|Other; Comment=CommentViolation. CommentViolationCategory is required for Comment: SpamAdvertising|HarassmentHate|PrivacyThreat|CoordinatedManipulation|Other; Admin independently determines the confirmed category. DuplicateLocation requires DuplicateOfLocationId FK Location (RESTRICT), distinct visible canonical target, and null feature/submission/comment/proposed-pin fields; index this FK. Store reported comment/version snapshot privately. Shared Description is trimmed 10–1500 characters. IDs, actor, timestamps, status, versions, verdict and penalty are backend-controlled.
Keep resolution reason/outcome as private moderation metadata, never as a public feature value. ReportStatusHistory: Id UUID v4 PK; ReportId FK; FromStatus nullable; ToStatus required; ActorId FK; Reason/Outcome text where applicable; OccurredAt UTC. A submitted report and its first history row are inserted in the same transaction. Existing LocationFeature and Submission rows are referenced, not copied. LocationMetadataHistory stores immutable old/new Location metadata snapshots and source/version.
A correction locks the Location, checks expectedVersion, commits new values and history atomically; rejected requests never change the pin. ReportEvidence is append-only: Id UUID v4 PK, ReportId FK (RESTRICT), AddedByReporterId FK, Description bounded nullable, LinkedSubmissionId nullable UUID FK → Submission.Id (nonblank Description or LinkedSubmissionId required), LinkedSubmissionRevision integer nullable, EvidenceSnapshotJson jsonb NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}', CreatedAt UTC, SourceVersion, IdempotencyKey and RequestHash. LinkedSubmissionId and LinkedSubmissionRevision are both null or both present; a present revision is positive and belongs to that Submission. The server freezes the exact revision's relevant immutable claim IDs and media IDs/hashes in EvidenceSnapshotJson under a versioned schema; description-only evidence stores {}. The client cannot supply or replace this snapshot. Enforce reporter = Report.ReporterId. A linked Submission must be owned by that reporter and resolve to the same canonical Location; a scoped feature report also requires matching ScopeId and the relevant claim.
Link only Submitted, AIProcessing, AwaitingMoreInfo, PendingModeration or Published attempts; linking pending evidence never proves its quality or publication outcome. Reject a new link to Rejected/Cancelled or superseded attempts. A metadata-only report may supply description without fabricating a WF1 feature claim. Accept no staged mediaIds, raw bytes or arbitrary media URLs on report supplements. Unique(ReportId, AddedByReporterId, IdempotencyKey) and Index(ReportId, CreatedAt, Id) support replay and audit.
The shared IdempotencyRecord (user, endpoint, key) stores the exact response and canonical body hash; same key/body replays without a new evidence row or history edge, changed body returns 409. Lock Report and check expectedVersion before append; evidence, status transition, version increment, history and outbox commit atomically. One accepted supplement creates exactly one ReportEvidence row with its own immutable LinkedSubmissionId and/or Description. Do not copy media rows or silently overwrite Report.LinkedSubmissionId/current correction selection; Admin explicitly links the appropriate correction, while prior supplement links remain in history.
Each supplement belongs to the report owner and canonical Location; linked source evidence stays under WF1 ownership and access rules. Do not edit the original Report description or count a supplement as a vote. A successful supplement in AwaitingMoreInfo atomically appends evidence, history and version, returns to UnderReview and notifies Admin; other states return 409.
B.22.2 Indexes, versioning and retention
Create an index on (LocationId, Status, CreatedAt DESC) for the admin queue and (ReporterId, CreatedAt DESC, Id DESC) for owner history; an optional filtered (LocationId, FeatureType, Status) index can support active-case triage after query plans justify it. Use the existing IdempotencyRecord contract keyed by user, endpoint and Idempotency-Key, with request hash and stored response; do not create a second uncoordinated idempotency table. Use Report.Version or an equivalent PostgreSQL concurrency token on every admin transition. Never hard-delete report/status history while an audit or linked dispute must be retained. Define retention and private-media expiry using the project's existing privacy policy; this section does not invent a public retention period.
B.22.3 POST request and response contract
POST /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/reports requires Bearer and Idempotency-Key. IncorrectFeature example: {"reason":"IncorrectFeature","scopeId":"<scope-uuid>","featureType":"Ramp","locationFeatureId":"<feature-uuid>","observedFeatureVersion":3,"targetSubmissionId":"<published-source-submission-uuid>","targetSubmissionClaimId":"<published-source-claim-uuid>","description":"Ramp information appears outdated","linkedSubmissionId":null}. Server validates all target IDs against the scoped published version. TargetSubmissionId/TargetSubmissionClaimId identify reported source evidence; LinkedSubmissionId is optional separately owned correction evidence, never a substitute target. MissingFeature may name the scope and absent feature with null published target/version. Place-level WrongAddressOrPin uses Location as target: {"reason":"WrongAddressOrPin","description":"Entrance pin is on adjacent building","proposedAddress":"<address>","proposedPosition":{"latitude":10.77,"longitude":106.70},"linkedSubmissionId":null}. Proposed values require Admin approval before Location changes. Comment report uses the same endpoint and idempotency/rate-limit contract with {targetType:"Comment",commentId:"<comment-uuid>",reportedCommentVersion:1,reason:"CommentViolation",description:"Reason for reporting this comment"}. Require a publicly visible comment in the same canonical Location at creation; retain its private snapshot if later hidden. Comment supplements accept description only and reject linkedSubmissionId. Derive ReporterId from the token. First success returns 201 with reportId/status/locationId/createdAt; identical replay returns the stored response and changed payload returns 409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED. Submission example: {targetType:"Submission",targetSubmissionId:"<published-submission-uuid>",reason:"MisleadingEvidence",description:"Describe the published evidence issue"}; optional targetSubmissionClaimId narrows the target. Duplicate example: {targetType:"Location",reason:"DuplicateLocation",duplicateOfLocationId:"<other-location-uuid>",description:"Explain why these are the same physical place"}. User chooses a fixed CommentViolationCategory for a comment report. No report creation hides a comment, merges places or establishes a violation.
B.22.4 Read and moderation API contract
GET /api/v1/me/reports?pageSize&cursor returns only the authenticated reporter's reportId, safe location name, optional featureType, status, createdAt, last public-safe update and nextCursor; never include other reporters or private review notes. GET /api/v1/admin/reports?status&locationId&cursor requires isAdmin=true, validated Admin Portal session/scope and Wf02.Moderate, returns a bounded queue with author reference, target/version, reason and authorized evidence references. PATCH /api/v1/admin/reports/{reportId} requires a typed decision, reason and expectedVersion: {"decision":"RequestEvidence","note":"Provide a current entrance photo","expectedVersion":2}. Response includes reportId, status, version and updatedAt; stale expectedVersion returns 409 REPORT_VERSION_CHANGED with a safe current summary. Unsupported transitions return 409 INVALID_REPORT_TRANSITION; malformed input returns 422. The server records admin identity from auth, not request data, and applies B.22.7's conflict guard to the reporter, challenged source contributor, linked correction contributor and linked dispute voters before any decision. GET /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/timeline?pageSize&cursor returns approved redacted LocationMetadataHistory and scoped published LocationFeatureHistory in effective-time order, resolving merges with a stable cursor. GET /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/comments?pageSize&cursor returns Approved CommunityComments newest first; POST /api/v1/locations/{locationId}/comments creates PendingReview content for its author. Admin comment approval/hide requires reason and history. Comment reports appear in the existing report queue with TargetType=Comment and CommentId; owner reads expose only safe status. Confirmed violation resolution records violation category, evidence, reason and the reviewed standing sanction under the versioned WF4 policy. Resolve the report, append its decision and comment moderation history when applicable, and persist one durable conduct event atomically. Routine hiding does not itself authorize a penalty. No public route exposes vote comments or raw reports. Admin metadata contract: PATCH /api/v1/admin/locations/{locationId}/metadata accepts proposedAddress/position, sourceReportId, expectedMetadataVersion and reason. It validates the report/canonical Location and neighboring identity, locks Location, updates address/position and MetadataVersion, writes before/after LocationMetadataHistory and resolves the source report with MetadataCorrected in one transaction. On stale version return 409 with no partial update. Entrance-anchor correction delegates to WF-01's authorized AccessScope position service; the report decision links its resulting history version. POST /api/v1/me/reports/{reportId}/evidence requires the authenticated report owner, Idempotency-Key and expectedVersion; body is {expectedVersion, description?, linkedSubmissionId?}; require nonblank description and/or one owned WF1 Submission UUID. Reject mediaIds, OwnedMediaId, raw file and URL fields. Media is uploaded/submitted through WF1 first and then linked, never attached directly to ReportEvidence. B.22.1 defines the authoritative supplement schema and ownership/location/scope checks. Only AwaitingMoreInfo accepts it; exact replay returns the same evidence result, a changed payload with the same key or a stale version returns 409, foreign report returns 403/404. Response includes reportId, evidenceId, linkedSubmissionId (nullable), status: UnderReview, version and action timestamp. Authorized matching-key replay is resolved before current-state/version checks; new supplements require AwaitingMoreInfo and the current expectedVersion. GET /api/v1/me/reports/{reportId} includes the Admin's public-safe requested detail and the owner's supplements. POST /api/v1/admin/locations/{locationId}/comments/{commentId}/moderation approves or hides a pending/approved public comment with expectedVersion and reason; audit actor/time/old/new state. Public comment GET defaults to newest-first by server-side CreatedAt then Id, with a stable cursor; approved comments also have read-time CommentRecencyWeight under the versioned 30-day initial half-life. The response marks an approved comment isRecentContext=true when its read-time weight is at least 0.25; the client highlights at most the first three such comments on the first page as a recent-context preview. Otherwise it shows no preview. There is no relevance-sort parameter in the MVP; older approved comments remain visible.
B.22.5 Validation matrix and ownership rules
Validate UUIDs, authentication, active/canonical Location, supported reason, feature enum, bounded nonempty description, observed feature version when supplied, linked Submission ownership and same canonical Location. A missing feature must not be rejected solely because no LocationFeature exists. An observed version mismatch may be accepted as a historical report with a stale-baseline flag for admin review; it must never be counted as a current-version vote. Reject foreign linked Submission IDs with 403/404 according to the existing non-disclosure policy. Apply user/Location rate limits and duplicate hints; a similar report from another person is not silently discarded or counted as corroboration. No client standing, accuracy, reputation, moderation state, public media URL or award amount is trusted. Validate ScopeId belongs to canonical Location and matches referenced feature/version; WrongAddressOrPin proposed coordinates are finite, in range and retained as untrusted request data. Approved metadata correction uses a Location version guard and append-only before/after history; do not count coordinate reports as votes. Stage 1 checks auth/visibility, typed FK/version, fixed reason/category, 10–1500 text, limits and idempotency. Stage 2 requires uninvolved Admin evidence comparison and ConfirmedValid|ConfirmedInvalid|Inconclusive|Duplicate outcome, reason and action. Stage-1 acceptance is not verification. Submission reports include source contributor in conflict-of-interest checks. Duplicate issues use a canonical unordered pair key; repeated reports do not create independent rewards or sanctions.
B.22.6 Creation transaction and idempotency
Perform authentication and cheap request validation first. Resolve merged Location identity and authorized linked Submission outside any long transaction. In one short PostgreSQL transaction: check IdempotencyRecord and hash; lock/recheck the canonical Location and linked subject as needed; insert Report at Submitted with Version=1; insert first ReportStatusHistory; store replayable 201 response and an optional notification outbox entry; commit. Return the response after commit. Any notification or external media lookup runs outside the transaction. If the process fails before commit, nothing is visible; if it fails after commit but before responding, replay retrieves the same report. Concurrent identical keys yield at most one Report through a unique idempotency constraint and conflict recovery.
B.22.7 State transition guards and admin actions
Allowed report transitions: Submitted→UnderReview/Rejected; UnderReview→AwaitingMoreInfo/LinkedToDispute/Resolved/Rejected; AwaitingMoreInfo→UnderReview/Rejected; LinkedToDispute→UnderReview/Resolved. Resolved and Rejected are terminal for that Report. Each transition requires actor authorization, expectedVersion, reason and one append-only history row in the same transaction as the version increment. An Admin decision is forbidden when the authenticated Admin ID matches the Report.ReporterId, the contributor of the challenged TargetSubmission/current published baseline source, the contributor of a linked correction Submission, or any linked CommunityVote.VoterId reached through DisputeCaseVote.CommunityVoteId (including the originating vote); a report linked to a dispute inherits those case conflicts. For Comment targets, also compare the authenticated Admin with the comment author and reporter; another uninvolved Admin must decide. Comment reports cannot enter LinkedToDispute or trigger feature/advisory/metadata correction. Use ConfirmedValid, ConfirmedInvalid, Inconclusive or Duplicate for the report outcome; a standing penalty additionally requires an explicit confirmed conduct violation. A reviewed outcome correction on an already terminal report is a separate ReviseOutcome action: require priorDecisionId, new verificationOutcome/findingType, evidence, reason and expectedVersion, with current uninvolved Admin authority. Keep the terminal status, append a ReportStatusHistory decision superseding the prior one, increment Version and emit its source-linked revision event atomically. Do not overwrite old decisions or reopen the case. ClaimAssessment revisions remain a separate authorized claim-level decision using WF-04 B.1's revision endpoint; they never reopen a terminal report. Reversed comment sanctions compensate only the original standing effect once.
Resolve these identities against the canonical published source and locked case/version in the decision transaction. Another uninvolved Admin must decide; a rejected self-review attempt writes no transition or history row. A one-Admin case needing manual review remains pending without a self-approval exception. Linking a DisputeCase requires the same canonical Location and compatible feature/version context; link reuse does not create another case or a vote. Marking Resolved with outcome CorrectionPublished requires an existing, actually Published WF-01 Submission or publication/version reference; a pending correction can be linked but does not meet that outcome.
A review/advisory outcome requires the relevant WF-02 advisory record and expiry policy. No admin transition writes LocationFeature directly. Resolved outcome MetadataCorrected requires the same transaction to commit an approved versioned Location metadata update and immutable history row. Admin reviews target identity, evidence and neighboring-place ambiguity; community votes inform but never directly move the pin. For scoped feature cases, Report.ScopeId must match linked claim, feature version and dispute. DuplicateLocation is handed to WF1 merge preview/write. Record DuplicateMerged and its actual history/version only after an audited merge commits; otherwise keep review open. Identity-duplicate reports receive no standing/ranking reward and merge itself grants none. A factual report never directly changes accuracy; correcting the original claim outcome requires a separately authorized ClaimAssessment revision.
The AwaitingMoreInfo→UnderReview edge is initiated only by an owner supplement accepted under the report's current expectedVersion (or an explicit audited Admin reopening with existing evidence); its reason links ReportEvidenceId. RequestEvidence must specify the missing detail in the owner-safe response. A notification failure cannot undo the evidence/history transaction.
B.22.8 WF-01, vote and dispute integration
An optional linked WF-01 Submission must pass owner or admin authorization and point to the same canonical Location. WF-01 remains responsible for photo/video validation, AI verification, correction submission state and feature publication. WF-02 stores only its linked ID and safe derived context. A report can be linked to a DisputeCase for triage; it is not inserted into DisputeCaseVote and does not increase DistinctContributorCount or WeightedAgreement. If a separate CommunityVote is submitted by the same user, it has its own ID, idempotency key, eligibility and one-person rule. On WF-01 publication, reconcile linked report/case against the new feature version and require an auditable report outcome; do not automatically declare every related report true or award points. WF-04 receives only separately approved, reviewable events.
B.22.9 Notifications, visibility and privacy
Notify the reporter after a committed request for evidence or final decision using WF-01 B.3.17 outbox/FCM. Set PayloadJson.sourceType=InaccurateInformationReport, sourceId=Report.Id, reportId=Report.Id and sourceEventId=the committed ReportStatusHistory.Id; no linked Submission or DisputeCase is required for a standalone report. Validate the source and owner before committing. Delivery retry must not duplicate ReportStatusHistory. Show the reporter a safe status and action required, but hide private admin deliberation, another user's report and raw GPS/media metadata. Admin evidence access uses authorized short-lived private media links and existing privacy/blur rules. Logs include correlation ID, reportId, actorId, transition and error category, but not full description, sensitive media URL or provider token. WF-03 search may offer an explicit Report action; it never submits one during search or publishes report text as accessibility truth.
B.22.10 Failure, race and recovery outcomes
Case R-01 duplicate identical POST: replay 201 body, one Report and one first history row. R-02 same key changed payload: 409, no second report. R-03 target merged concurrently: retry canonical resolution or return 409 with safe replacement identity; never attach to two Locations. R-04 feature version changes after report submission: retain the report and observed version for historical review; do not reclassify it as a new vote. R-05 two admins update from Version=2: exactly one commits; the other receives 409 and reloads. R-06 evidence Submission rejected/cancelled: unlink unusable evidence only through an audited admin transition; keep the report. R-07 FCM delivery or dispatcher/Hangfire scheduling fails after commit: report/history and its durable outbox row remain committed; reconciliation retries delivery. A required outbox DB insert belongs to the source transaction, so its DB failure cannot leave a source falsely committed without the required notification record. R-08 WF-01 correction fails or is pending: retain the report in review/linked state; never claim CorrectionPublished. R-09 rate limit: 429 with retry guidance and no partially persisted report.
B.22.11 Integration tests and release gates
Test report of an existing feature and of a missing feature; place-level report; merged Location resolution; owner-only list versus admin queue; valid and foreign Submission linkage; stale observed version; same-key replay and changed-key conflict; concurrent report creation; concurrent admin decisions; self-review rejection for an Admin's own report, challenged published Submission, any linked dispute vote (including a non-originating vote) and linked correction, a second uninvolved Admin's valid decision, and one-Admin pending behavior; verify a concurrent source/case link cannot bypass the guard; all allowed and forbidden transitions; dispute coalescing; a report plus vote by the same user counted only once as a vote; no Report affecting WF-01 community-agreement contribution; pending versus Published correction outcome; outbox outage; audit/PII/media-link exposure.
Database assertions inspect ReportStatusHistory, Version, IdempotencyRecord and unchanged LocationFeature/CommunityAssessment. Done means the API, schema, authorization, race handling and business outcomes above are observable and reproducible; tier multipliers and auto-resolution are excluded from the baseline; reviewed standing sanctions follow WF4 v3-metrics-3, not an open penalty policy. Add wrong-address/pin report and concurrent Admin corrections (one version wins), unchanged prior capture snapshots, scope mismatch rejection, public timeline redaction/pagination/merged Location, newest approved comments, private vote-comment isolation and recent-context emphasis that never changes LocationFeature.
Test description-only, linkedSubmissionId-only and combined supplements, stale version, identical replay after the state/version changed, changed payload with the same key, foreign owner, wrong state, concurrent Admin decision, missing/foreign/wrong-Location/wrong-scope or superseded/Rejected/Cancelled Submission links and outbox outage. Reject raw/staged media fields. Pending linked evidence cannot resolve CorrectionPublished; actual qualifying publication is required. Preserve every supplement link without replacing prior evidence.
Verify one ReportEvidence row, one state-history edge and no CommunityVote/LocationFeature mutation. For Comment reports test same-Location FK/version, private snapshot, ownership, self-review rejection, idempotent retries, later-hidden comments and concurrent decisions. Pending, duplicate, inconclusive and honestly rejected reports produce no score effect. A confirmed violation deducts only the accountable user's standing once per violation regardless of report count; no reporter reward, ReputationPoints change, claim-counter change or confidence change. An overturned decision restores only the originally applied standing deduction once. Factual reports likewise never change claim counters directly; a separately revised claim assessment is required. Test Admin comment approval/hide with version and audit; default public newest-first stable pagination, private notes excluded, and read-time comment decay at day 0, 30 and 60 (weights 1, 0.5 and 0.25 under the initial 30-day half-life). Verify the 0.25 recent-context boundary, at most three preview comments, no preview when all approved comments are older, older comments remain reachable, no relevance-sort parameter, and no LocationFeature or vote mutation. Verify typed Submission/Comment/Duplicate targets and reason allowlists, description boundaries9/10/1500/1501, target visibility, comment snapshot, stale target versions and same-Location links. Test comment penalties −2/−4/−6 only after explicit Admin confirmation, no automatic penalty for hiding/reporting, one penalty across many reports, malicious-report −4, one applied-amount reversal and unchanged accuracy/reputation/confidence. Test duplicate report cannot itself merge or reward.
Verify a standalone report with no Submission/DisputeCase can notify its owner using reportId plus its history sourceEventId. Replay creates one outbox event; a later distinct evidence request creates another. Reject missing/mismatched source context. Check dispute transitions from every permitted starting status and replacement of a PendingValidation vote by a newer same-user observation.
Outbox assertions: PayloadJson.reportId/sourceId equal Report.Id and sourceEventId equals that report's committed ReportStatusHistory.Id, not the report ID copied into every field. Replayed decisions emit one logical notification; another audited decision gets its own history source.
B.23 Definition of Done
WF-02 is complete when authenticated users can submit idempotent feature-specific votes and separate detailed Reports; admins can audit/version report decisions and feature disputes, link only real WF-01 corrections, and never count Reports as votes. Hangfire reliably maintains separate freshness/community read models, temporary advisories expire safely, and all history remains auditable without changing WF-01 confidence or published truth on a quick vote or Report. The SQL schema, DTOs, authorization, privacy, migration and test scenarios in B.3–B.22 are required gates; the Report API and state transitions in B.22 are included. A.17 records the selected baseline and explicitly deferred extensions; it is not an open choice for a coding agent. Use WF4 v3-metrics-3 sanctions and weights, Admin-only case resolution and the disabled cross-source integration gate. External deployment inputs and calibration artefacts must pass their owning readiness checks.
